# Architecture and workflow

Git documentation and source code are the source of truth. Never use previous chat history.

Before any task, read `PROJECT_DEVELOPMENT_RULES.md`, `PROJECT_STATUS.md`, `SPRINT_STATUS.md`, `CURRENT_TASK.md`, then relevant docs and this rules folder.

Work only on the task in `CURRENT_TASK.md`. Never start the next task automatically.

Workflow: Plan → Implement → Test → Review → Document → Update status → Commit → Stop.

## Layers

- Domain: no Next.js, React, SQL, Tailwind, or provider SDKs.
- Application: use cases; depends on domain and repository interfaces only.
- Infrastructure: static/mock repos and the dummy API client now; server-only
  provider adapters and any approved persistence only in their scheduled tasks.
- UI/HTTP: thin pages and Route Handlers.

One Next.js application owns UI and server-side code (ADR 0006); no separate
backend service.

Current: `Next.js → Application → Repository interface → HTTP repository →
in-process dummy API → static data`.
Planned: same interfaces; implementation selected in `config/` → Mini Mystiq
API contract → dummy or server-only Zoho adapter (cache/snapshot, ADR 0009).

Do not rewrite the storefront when replacing mock repositories with API repositories.

## Phase guardrails

- Storefront is mobile-first (Mobile → Tablet → Desktop). Admin may be desktop-priority but must stay responsive.
- No separate backend service (ADR 0006). No database unless ADR 0008 is
  amended and accepted. Zoho waits for Sprint 7 and verified access. No admin,
  cart, checkout, or payments without an explicit task.
- Do not initialize Next.js or install packages unless the current task says so.
- Significant architecture changes require an ADR in `docs/decisions/`.
- Undecided business facts are TBD. Do not invent them.

After every completed task, update `CURRENT_TASK.md`, `PROJECT_STATUS.md`, `SPRINT_STATUS.md`, and the sprint file.
